 "$comment": "Named oil and gas producing regions, authored for OpenDoctrines. Replaces ACOR (ETH Zurich), which ships no licence and is itself a digitisation of a 1982 atlas -- see NOTICE.md. Nothing here is copied from ACOR or from any other dataset: each entry is a named region with an approximate centre and a weight chosen for play balance. `fields` is expanded by load_oil_fields() into that many points, which is what the diminishing-returns curve in scale_resource() consumes. `iso` is required and is what the region is attributed to -- over half these centres are at sea, where the map has no province to read a country off, so placement matches the nearest province OF THAT COUNTRY rather than the nearest province. `offshore` is documentation for the reader; the code does not branch on it. `iso_fallback` lists countries to try when the map does not model `iso` at all -- a 2000-start map has no South Sudan or Timor-Leste, and their oil should go to whoever held the ground then rather than vanish. Map-independent: on a map that does model them, the fallback is never reached.",
